#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:16
msgid ""
"Use `T.copy(src, dst, *, coalesced_width=None, disable_tma=False, "
"eviction_policy=None, loop_layout=None)` to move tiles between memory "
"scopes. It accepts `tir.Buffer`, `BufferLoad`, or `BufferRegion`; extents "
"are inferred or broadcast when possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:20
msgid ""
"# Global → Shared tiles (extents inferred from dst)\n"
"T.copy(A[by * BM, ko * BK], A_s)\n"
"T.copy(B[ko * BK, bx * BN], B_s)\n"
"\n"
"# Fragment/Register → Global (store result)\n"
"T.copy(C_f, C[by * BM, bx * BN])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:29
msgid "Semantics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:30
msgid ""
"Extents are deduced from arguments; missing sides broadcast to the other’s "
"rank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:31
msgid ""
"Access patterns are legalized and coalesced during lowering. Explicit "
"vectorization is not required in HL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:33
msgid ""
"Safety: the LegalizeSafeMemoryAccess pass inserts boundary guards when an "
"access may be out‑of‑bounds and drops them when proven safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:36
msgid "Lowering `T.copy` to variants of copy mechanisms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:38
msgid "TileLang supports both synchronous and explicitly-asynchronous copies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:40
msgid "`T.copy(src, dst, ...)` (synchronous semantics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:41
msgid "Intended default for most TileLang programs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:42
msgid ""
"The compiler is free to lower it to different mechanisms (synchronous SIMT "
"copy `ld.global`, warp-level copy     `ldmatrix`, async copy via TMA `cp."
"async.bulk`, old async copy `cp.async`, etc.) depending on target/hints, but "
"the   observable semantics are *synchronous*: after the statement, it is "
"safe to use `dst`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:44
msgid ""
"If `T.copy` lowers to `cp.async`, TileLang will still preserve synchronous "
"semantics by emitting the required `commit`/`wait` (and any required "
"synchronization) so that consuming `dst` is correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:48
msgid "`T.async_copy(src, dst, ...)` (explicit async semantics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:49
msgid ""
"Intended for writing manual pipelines or warp-specialized code where you "
"want to overlap global->shared copies with compute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:51
msgid "Lowers through `cp.async` and emits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:52
msgid "`ptx_cp_async(...)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:53
msgid "`ptx_commit_group()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:54
msgid "No `ptx_wait_group(...)` is auto-inserted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:55
msgid ""
"You must explicitly insert `T.ptx_wait_group(...)` before consuming `dst`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:56
msgid ""
"A barrier is still required when `dst` is produced cooperatively and "
"consumed across threads. In most TileLang programs you do not need to write "
"it manually: `ThreadSync(\"shared\")` will insert the required `T."
"tvm_storage_sync(\"shared\")` before the first read from `dst`. If you want "
"explicit control (or if you're writing very low-level code), you can insert "
"`T.tvm_storage_sync(\"shared\")` yourself (or `T.tvm_storage_sync(\"warp\")` "
"for warp-local consumption)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:63
msgid ""
"This op is intentionally strict: if the copy cannot be lowered to `cp.async` "
"(e.g., wrong scopes, unsupported vector width), compilation fails instead of "
"silently falling back to a synchronous copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:67
msgid "Example (manual async prefetch)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:68
msgid ""
"# Prefetch into shared asynchronously (emits cp.async + commit).\n"
"T.async_copy(A[by * BM, ko * BK], A_s)\n"
"\n"
"# ... independent work here ...\n"
"\n"
"# Before consuming A_s, ensure the async copies are completed.\n"
"T.ptx_wait_group(0)\n"
"# The required shared-memory barrier will be inserted automatically before "
"the\n"
"# first read from A_s by ThreadSync(\"shared\") in the default lowering "
"pipeline.\n"
"T.gemm(A_s, B_s, C_f)\n"
msgstr ""

