#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:197
msgid "Warp-vote / warp-ballot (CUDA ≥ 9 / HIP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:198
msgid ""
"`T.any_sync(predicate[, mask])` → `int32`: Non-zero if ANY lane in `mask` "
"has non-zero predicate (`__any_sync`). `mask` defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:199
msgid ""
"`T.all_sync(predicate[, mask])` → `int32`: Non-zero if ALL lanes in `mask` "
"have non-zero predicate (`__all_sync`). `mask` defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:200
msgid ""
"`T.ballot_sync(predicate[, mask])` → `uint64`: Bitmask of lanes in `mask` "
"with non-zero predicate. CUDA: `__ballot_sync` zero-extended to 64 bits; "
"HIP: `__ballot` returns natively as `uint64`, covering all 64 wavefront "
"lanes. `mask` defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:201
msgid ""
"`T.ballot(predicate)` → `uint64`: Full-warp/wavefront ballot (mask = "
"`0xFFFFFFFF`). No truncation on HIP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:202
msgid ""
"`T.activemask()` → `uint64`: Bitmask of currently active lanes. CUDA: "
"`__activemask` zero-extended to 64 bits; HIP: `__ballot(1)` as `uint64`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:204
msgid "Block-wide predicated sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:205
msgid ""
"`T.syncthreads_count(predicate)` → `int32`: Sync all threads; return count "
"with non-zero predicate (`__syncthreads_count`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:206
msgid ""
"`T.syncthreads_and(predicate)` → `int32`: Sync; non-zero iff ALL threads "
"have non-zero predicate (`__syncthreads_and`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:207
msgid ""
"`T.syncthreads_or(predicate)` → `int32`: Sync; non-zero iff ANY thread has "
"non-zero predicate (`__syncthreads_or`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:209
msgid ""
"Warp-shuffle (intra-warp data exchange). All accept a trailing `mask` kwarg "
"that defaults to `0xFFFFFFFF`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:210
msgid ""
"`T.shfl_sync(value, src_lane[, width, mask])`: Broadcast value from "
"`src_lane` to all lanes (`__shfl_sync`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:211
msgid ""
"`T.shfl_xor(value, delta[, width, mask])`: XOR-swap across lanes "
"(`__shfl_xor_sync`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:212
msgid ""
"`T.shfl_down(value, delta[, width, mask])`: Shift down by `delta` lanes "
"(`__shfl_down_sync`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:213
msgid ""
"`T.shfl_up(value, delta[, width, mask])`: Shift up by `delta` lanes "
"(`__shfl_up_sync`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:215
msgid ""
"Warp-match (CUDA sm_70+, not supported on HIP). `mask` defaults to "
"`0xFFFFFFFF`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:216
msgid ""
"`T.match_any_sync(value[, mask])` → `uint32`: Bitmask of lanes in `mask` "
"whose `value` matches the calling lane's (`__match_any_sync`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:217
msgid ""
"`T.match_all_sync(value[, mask])` → `uint32`: Returns `mask` if all lanes in "
"`mask` agree on `value`, else 0 (`__match_all_sync`). The C-level `int*` "
"predicate output is hidden; reconstruct it as `result != 0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/instructions.md:219
msgid ""
"**Note on HIP:** `any_sync`/`all_sync` ignore the mask and call `__any`/"
"`__all` directly. `ballot_sync`, `ballot`, and `activemask` call `__ballot` "
"which returns `uint64` natively on 64-thread wavefronts — no truncation "
"occurs. Shuffle intrinsics lower to `__shfl`/`__shfl_xor`/`__shfl_down`/"
"`__shfl_up` (mask ignored). `syncthreads_count/and/or` have identical "
"signatures on both platforms. `match_any_sync` and `match_all_sync` have no "
"HIP equivalent and will fail to codegen on HIP."
msgstr ""

